('E1',P,'135-193; 260-339','Direct normalization, exact moments and standard-deviation units','Mf.DP.sampledGaussianSourceProductLaw_map_positiveGaussianScale; Mf.DP.sampledGaussianReferenceProductLaw_map_positiveGaussianScale; Mf.DP.integral_sparseGaussianProductLikelihoodRatio_sq_belowBox','X Finding 2; Y Findings 2-3','supported/faithful correspondence','correct correspondence/control','The two laws use coordinate variance sigma^2. Division by positive sigma sends the reference to standard Gaussian and the source to the uncentered sparse mixture at mu=Delta/sigma. Exact product moments and Gaussian tilt yield the displayed pP, pQ and m2; both sign-unrestricted real shift and arbitrary finite horizon are retained. This control supplements C4 and does not turn a matched mean Gaussian into the privacy reference.','Useful for interpreting likelihood/moment formulas and scale units.','No independent kernel or axiom replay.'),
('E2',K,'65-69','Euclidean clipping and vector Gaussian scale','Mf.DP.l2Norm; Mf.DP.l2VectorClip_norm_le; Mf.DP.bsrGaussianMeasure','X Finding 1; Y Finding 2','supported/faithful correspondence','correct correspondence/control','The raw coordinate functions are mapped to EuclideanSpace via WithLp.toLp 2 before taking their norm; the unit specialization bounds the L2 norm. FiniteGaussian.measure delegates to independent coordinate Gaussian laws at the real scale. Source sigma>0 is inside the formal scale domain.','Useful prevention of a sup-norm or variance/standard-deviation substitution; included in C1 consequence rather than an independent primary discovery.','No independent compilation.'),
