('E4',P,'544-580','Numerical illustration as approximate arithmetic','Finite formulas in sparseGaussianProductMaximumEventForwardLowerBoundReal and sparseGaussianProductForwardCappedRestrictedSecondMomentUpperBoundReal; no concrete replay declaration mapped','X Finding 6; Y Finding 6','supported/faithful correspondence','correct correspondence/control','Bounded local double-precision substitution independently reproduces lower 0.1000288274320239, forward upper 0.09945249723725613, reverse dual 0.052593966541184756, reverse floor 0, width 6.461454477027124 percent. This supports displayed rounding only; it cannot certify rational intervals, independently supplied PLD, or the report Y arbitrary-precision implementation details.','Useful limited transcription control; no formal numeric or executable calibration authority.','The report numerical scripts are not part of INPUT; their exact method and claimed extra precision cannot be independently attested. See evidence/bounded_checks.py and stdout.'),
('E5',K,'226-251; 379-400','Fallback arithmetic, degeneracies and ideal-law scope','No full KOutOfT fallback theorem mapped; source elementary arithmetic and mechanism definition inspected','X Finding 6; Y inventory D 226-251 and D 379-407','supported/faithful correspondence','correct correspondence/control','For k>=0 and delta>0, (k+1)/delta>0 and k*delta/(2*(k+1))<=delta. This checks arithmetic conditional on the stated Gaussian comparison, not the absent checker. At k=0 the transcript law is dataset-independent; for epsilon>=0 and delta>=1 every probability-law profile is <=delta. Thus all positive scales are feasible and infimum zero is not a least positive scale. The exclusions in positive-threshold clauses are appropriate.','Useful limitation of finite-family minimality, positive-threshold domains and mathematical versus runtime scope.','Full fallback comparison and actual checker soundness are not independently discharged.'),
('E6',K,'88-113; 191-251; 327-344','Total finite exact-rational calibrator and uniform add/remove reduction','Unresolved mapping: missing KOutOfT CandidateChecker, TotalAccountant, RequestOnlyUpperCalibration, TrainingReduction owners','X abstention 1; Y A1','unresolved','warranted abstention','The source requires a total rational algorithm, finite accepted-family minimum and privacy for all record types, dimensions and measurable oracles. Only the transcript mechanism is supplied among 25 distinct cited KOutOfT note paths; 24 cited paths are absent. Static absence supports a capsule coverage limit and is not a proof of theorem failure. Mechanism normalization and fallback arithmetic do not imply universal adaptive privacy or algorithm termination.','Useful warranted boundary: neither report substitutes a loose fixed-oracle accountant or a definition for the stated universal theorem.','Mathematical theorem, termination and full reduction remain unverified; missing local sources do not resolve their ultimate truth.'),
('E7',K,'253-284; 346-376','Signed one-step domination and full adaptive direct replacement','Unresolved full mapping: signedHiddenGaussianStopLossDomination and direct replacement theorem not present as declarations in local sources','X abstention 2; Y A2','unresolved','warranted abstention','The stated norm constraint gives |<m_h,m_g>|<=|a_h*a_g|. If all W_h*a_h share a sign, W_h*W_g*a_h*a_g>=|W_h*W_g*<m_h,m_g>|, so the displayed compensated quadratic summands are nonnegative; zero amplitudes imply zero means. Positive multipliers preserve that sign argument. This is conditional algebra, not a proof of the interpolation derivative, smoothing convergence or adaptive backward comparison with history-dependent future factors. Reports correctly preserve all these larger obligations and do not claim a refutation.','Useful method distinction: a one-step sign calculation and a complete sequential theorem are different obligations. No unsupported false claim or substituted two-hop adjacency result is asserted.','Full measurable interpolation and adaptive extension remain unresolved. The terse prose may be completable, but local absence and the analysis here do not decide it.'),
('E8',K,'286-323; 334-376','Lower realizations and positive attained uniform thresholds','Unresolved KOutOfT profile/lower-realization/threshold mappings; generic Mf.DP.Training.IsGlobalSigmaThreshold is not a KOutOfT instance','X abstention 3; Y A3','unresolved','warranted abstention','The truncated feasible-set infimum argument is coherent conditional on profile continuity, monotonicity, nonempty feasibility and a positive infeasible scale under 0<k<=T and 0<delta<1. Positive scalar +1 and signed +/-1 oracle projections require explicit pushforward identities for the padded history; those are not established by the available definition alone. No Poisson infimum theorem can replace this fixed-cardinality, attained, universally quantified statement.','Useful warranted abstention preserving the original domain and quantifier order.','Exact profile facts, lower-realization pushforwards and concrete positive attained thresholds remain unverified.'),
('E9',P,'646-669; 673-674; 715-716','Finite rational interval replay and historical replay provenance','Unresolved local mapping: Mf.DP.sampledGaussian_calibration_interval_of_finiteBracket_replayCertificate; abstract paired-certificate adapter present','X abstention 4; Y A4','unresolved','warranted abstention','The note explicitly requires exact outward CDF/exponential enclosures and squared rational square-root bounds. Such containments would support the arithmetic adapter, but no concrete rational certificate is in the supplied packet and the named replay declaration is absent from the local declaration inventory. This does not contradict the supplied abstract calibration theorem, establish absence from another project, or refute earlier working-tree replay. Report-specific axiom prints and process logs are withheld, so their historical provenance is not independently attested here.','Useful separation of an abstract correct certificate theorem from actual numerical replay and past process assertions.','Concrete replay and historical axiom/build claims remain unresolved; no mathematical falsehood inferred.'),
('E10',K,'140-161; 163-189','Hockey-stick calculus and bounded Gaussian-channel sketch','Unresolved exact full KOutOfT decoder mapping; conventional source arguments examined','X inventory K 140-189; Y inventory D 142-189','supported/faithful correspondence','correct correspondence/control','For probability laws, test pullback proves data processing and common-weight mixtures by linearity and supremum. A measurable orthogonal map sending e0 to the padded vector (sqrt(1-||v||^2),v) gives the displayed one-step means and covariance for ||v||<=1 and sigma>0; dimension zero is harmless. This supports the reports stated conventional calculation. A complete recursive path-law endpoint is unavailable and both reports limit that stronger conclusion.','Useful conditional argument review; neither implies certified whole-note adaptive reduction.','Joint measurability can be obtained by a piecewise Householder choice, but no full recursive Lean owner was replayed. Assessment is of the described calculation with its stated limitation.'),
('E11',P,'592-644; 581-590','External literature, optimizer, PLD and runtime claims','No source-to-formal mapping claimed for external/runtime facts','X inventory bibliography/scope and Finding 6; Y A5','unresolved','warranted abstention','The reports explicitly exclude bibliographic authority, independent PLD calculation, optimizer behavior and finite-precision/application runtime conformance. The note itself limits its theorem to ideal independent product laws and calls decimals illustrative. Nothing in the supplied Lean profile theorems proves those external claims. No outside sources were consulted.','Useful scope boundary; no primary finding and no supported external factual conclusion.','External and runtime claims intentionally unverified.'),
('E12',K,'402-406','Training historical replay and endpoint axiom provenance','No mapping for absent training endpoint replay artifacts','X abstention 4 and inventory K 379-406; Y A4','unresolved','warranted abstention','The note historical working-tree replay claim cannot be reconstructed from the restricted source closure. Available definitions or a generic axiom statement do not attest a previous replay of absent theorem owners. Both reports explicitly refrain from such certification.','Useful provenance boundary, separate from source theorem truth.','Prior replay and complete endpoint axiom provenance remain unverified.')
